```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "fault_kind": "application_exception",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT service_name, count(*) n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND message LIKE '%threw exception%URI is not absolute%' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Travel-plan logs a SEVERE 'URI is not absolute' unhandled exception on nearly every request during the incident (1940 times)."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) errs, avg(duration)/1e6 avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND span_name LIKE 'POST /api/v1/travelplanservice%' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "All travel-plan POST endpoints (cheapest, minStation, quickest) return HTTP 500 with Error status in about 5ms, with no downstream child calls."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) errs, avg(duration)/1e6 avg_ms FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND span_name LIKE 'POST /api/v1/travelplanservice%' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "In the normal period the same travel-plan endpoints had no error spans and took hundreds of milliseconds."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, sum(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) errs, avg(duration)/1e6 avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND span_name LIKE 'POST /api/v1/travelplanservice%' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "ui-dashboard's travelPlan requests fail with HTTP 500 after about 3.2 seconds, mirroring travel-plan's failures reaching users."}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

**Notes on the investigation**

- **Affected user path:** `ts-ui-dashboard` is the only entry service. Its three `/travelPlan/*` endpoints (cheapest, minStation, quickest) are the only ones with errors, and their error share rises to about 0.16 overall. Its other endpoints stay at 0 errors.
- **Fault origin:** `ts-travel-plan-service` returns HTTP 500 to every travel-plan request in about 5 ms. Its logs show the same unhandled `IllegalArgumentException: URI is not absolute` on every request, and the failing requests make no downstream calls. That points to an exception in its own code path, not to the network or DNS. The exact code cause is not visible in telemetry, so `application_exception` is my best-fit kind; the log text is closer to a malformed or unresolved target URL than to a driver error.
- **Route-plan-service is not the fault:** its spans disappear from the abnormal period, but its pod keeps emitting metrics. It is simply no longer called, because travel-plan fails before reaching it. Its metrics show no restart or new pod. I did not name it.
- **Other shifts ruled out:** the many services with 80–90% lower span counts (auth, route, config, order, and others) track a drop in overall load and show no error increase, so I did not name them. I also did not confirm the log-count and filesystem-usage spikes in travel-plan and the notification and delivery services in depth; they are consistent with error logging and queue-redeclare noise rather than separate root causes.
- **Limitation:** I did not run a separate check of container CPU or memory for travel-plan, and the evidence for the exact fault mechanism inside the service is limited to the log text.

